  "notes": "ざぶざぶ is an onomatopoeia describing the sound or motion of splashing through water. It suggests vigorous, repeated water movement.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ざぶざぶ（と）{洗|あら}う: to wash vigorously with water\n- ざぶざぶ（と）{歩|ある}く: to wade through water\n- ざぶざぶ（と）{渡|わた}る: to splash across (a river)\n\nCONTRAST WITH SIMILAR ONOMATOPOEIA:\n- じゃぶじゃぶ: similar splashing, often for wading or washing hands\n- ばしゃばしゃ: more violent, irregular splashing\n- ちゃぷちゃぷ: gentler, lighter splashing\n- ざぶん: a single big splash (jumping into water)\n\nGRAMMAR:\nUsed as an adverb, often with と: ざぶざぶと{川|かわ}を{渡|わた}る。",
